1
00:00:17,715 --> 00:00:20,500
X THE LEAGUE's Round 3 mission is...

2
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,340
Limit Break.

3
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:26,953
Your ranking this round depends
on how much you surpass

4
00:00:26,953 --> 00:00:28,643
your previous record.

5
00:00:28,643 --> 00:00:30,401
That gives the lower-ranked teams a chance

6
00:00:30,401 --> 00:00:33,581
to make a huge leap and turn everything around.

7
00:00:33,581 --> 00:00:36,201
When I heard about the Round 3 mission,
I was really excited.

8
00:00:36,201 --> 00:00:38,506
I think this is Team USA's biggest chance

9
00:00:38,506 --> 00:00:40,553
to take a big leap forward in the competition.

10
00:00:40,553 --> 00:00:44,470
[Lower-ranked teams are looking
to make a comeback]

11
00:00:44,470 --> 00:00:47,526
[While higher-ranked teams feel burdened]
I think we're at a huge disadvantage.

12
00:00:47,526 --> 00:00:53,687
We're the only country
that moved up from X2 to X1.

13
00:00:53,687 --> 00:00:55,922
We need to sell a lot more.

14
00:00:55,922 --> 00:00:58,443
And we're out of our high-ticket items now.

15
00:00:59,319 --> 00:01:02,471
[What will Team Korea do to break through?]

16
00:01:02,471 --> 00:01:04,412
[Kkakk Unni steps out as a problem solver]

17
00:01:04,412 --> 00:01:05,875
I really need to get a good deal.

18
00:01:05,875 --> 00:01:08,019
[Where is she heading early in the morning?]

19
00:01:08,019 --> 00:01:11,771
Today, I'm heading to Tudari's factory.

20
00:01:11,771 --> 00:01:13,682
[Starting off at the Cuckoo HQ]

21
00:01:13,682 --> 00:01:14,839
We will get even more customers.

22
00:01:14,839 --> 00:01:17,419
[Kkakk Unni goes everywhere to get a good deal]
This is going to end in our loss.

23
00:01:17,419 --> 00:01:21,928
If I were to satisfy at least one customer,
I need to make a move myself.

24
00:01:21,928 --> 00:01:23,406
This is a special deal for X THE LEAGUE.

25
00:01:23,406 --> 00:01:28,242
[Tireless legwork brought about special deals]
I got you a special deal for XTL.

26
00:01:28,242 --> 00:01:31,127
Tudari has never done a group buy before.

27
00:01:31,127 --> 00:01:34,449
So I'm going to be their first
group buy organizer.

28
00:01:34,449 --> 00:01:37,645
I'm going to get an unprecedented deal.

29
00:01:37,645 --> 00:01:40,729
That's why I came all the way down
to their factory in Seosan.

30
00:01:41,567 --> 00:01:44,168
[Kkakk Unni does the legwork with passion]

31
00:01:44,168 --> 00:01:46,373
I think we're almost there.

32
00:01:46,373 --> 00:01:47,818
We came all the way here from Seoul.

33
00:01:47,818 --> 00:01:50,343
We should make sure this negotiation goes well.

34
00:01:51,258 --> 00:01:53,618
How much discount are you thinking?

35
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:55,717
Oh, you know.

36
00:01:55,717 --> 00:01:57,952
To the point that Tudari will start
disliking me.

37
00:01:57,952 --> 00:01:59,172
Every 100 won counts.

38
00:01:59,172 --> 00:02:00,981
We came here for a reason.

39
00:02:00,981 --> 00:02:02,325
[Arrived with a firm resolution]

40
00:02:02,325 --> 00:02:03,925
It's huge.

41
00:02:06,746 --> 00:02:10,997
[Intense negotiation is about
to take place right here]

42
00:02:14,749 --> 00:02:17,669
[Someone is sitting by himself]

43
00:02:18,383 --> 00:02:22,786
[Waiting for Kkakk Unni]

44
00:02:22,786 --> 00:02:25,958
[Today's negotiation partner:
Tudari's division director]

45
00:02:28,663 --> 00:02:31,550
Hello, director.

46
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,373
I'm Kkakk Unni.

47
00:02:33,373 --> 00:02:36,128
When we talked on the phone,
we couldn't reach an agreement.

48
00:02:36,128 --> 00:02:39,722
So I came from Seoul
to visit you here in Seosan.

49
00:02:39,722 --> 00:02:41,961
We can get to the discussion right away.

50
00:02:41,961 --> 00:02:43,486
Before we start,

51
00:02:43,486 --> 00:02:46,975
we have prepared some food
for you to try first.

52
00:02:46,975 --> 00:02:48,177
Oh, we'll try them.

53
00:02:48,177 --> 00:02:50,154
[Trying the food first before negotiation]
Got it.

54
00:02:50,661 --> 00:02:52,645
[Their best menu, skewers, and chicken wings]

55
00:02:52,645 --> 00:02:55,654
First of all, they look great.

56
00:02:55,654 --> 00:02:57,599
[Best menu served proudly]
How did you know I'd come hungry?

57
00:02:57,599 --> 00:03:00,579
[The products to be negotiated today
fill the table]

58
00:03:00,579 --> 00:03:04,654
[Trying a mouthful]

59
00:03:06,736 --> 00:03:08,274
This is really good.

60
00:03:08,274 --> 00:03:11,268
You can't leave out skewers when it comes
to Tudari. Let me try this.

61
00:03:11,268 --> 00:03:15,327
This is a combination
of our best-selling skewers.

62
00:03:15,327 --> 00:03:17,404
So you can try each of them.

63
00:03:17,404 --> 00:03:18,770
This is very good.

64
00:03:18,770 --> 00:03:21,414
I mean, how can it be so juicy?

65
00:03:21,414 --> 00:03:26,218
It is so good that it just made me think
I should get an even better price.

66
00:03:26,218 --> 00:03:28,625
- Oh.
- I'm sure about this.

67
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:31,956
If it tastes that good,
maybe you don't have to get discounts.

68
00:03:31,956 --> 00:03:36,219
That's not true. I want as many customers
as possible to taste this.

69
00:03:36,219 --> 00:03:37,345
So I need more discounts.

70
00:03:37,345 --> 00:03:41,326
The division director seemed to be proud
of the products because they taste so good,

71
00:03:41,326 --> 00:03:43,605
and that's why he didn't want
to give more discounts,

72
00:03:43,605 --> 00:03:46,846
but in fact, because they taste good,
more customers should be able to taste them.

73
00:03:46,846 --> 00:03:48,596
That's why we need more discounts.

74
00:03:48,596 --> 00:03:50,417
To be honest, I came here today

75
00:03:50,417 --> 00:03:54,264
because I didn't think the price list
you gave me was good enough.

76
00:03:54,264 --> 00:03:58,457
- The Kimchi Udon was *** won.
- Yes.

77
00:03:58,457 --> 00:04:02,586
From the customer's point of view,
the price doesn't seem so attractive.

78
00:04:02,586 --> 00:04:06,471
[Kkakk Unni gets down to negotiation]
How much more of a discount could you give us?

79
00:04:06,471 --> 00:04:08,977
We could go down to *** won.

80
00:04:08,977 --> 00:04:12,667
I didn't come here to get that price.

81
00:04:12,667 --> 00:04:16,736
I came from Songdo, Incheon, too,
because I heard you were asking for too much.

82
00:04:16,736 --> 00:04:19,186
- You came from Songdo?
- I came from the headquarters.

83
00:04:19,186 --> 00:04:22,956
So, I can only go down to *** won.

84
00:04:22,956 --> 00:04:26,327
With a discount that small,
it wouldn't even cover my gas to get here.

85
00:04:26,327 --> 00:04:28,293
Then I'll pay for your gas.

86
00:04:28,293 --> 00:04:29,838
[A tough negotiator]
You will pay for my gas?

87
00:04:29,838 --> 00:04:32,168
Here is what I was thinking when I came here.

88
00:04:32,168 --> 00:04:34,918
I can minimize my profit.

89
00:04:34,918 --> 00:04:39,875
I want to give my followers and residents
the best deal they can get.

90
00:04:39,875 --> 00:04:43,515
That was what I was thinking.
I shared it with my employees, too.

91
00:04:44,015 --> 00:04:45,028
[Nods]

92
00:04:45,028 --> 00:04:46,397
[And?]

93
00:04:46,397 --> 00:04:48,225
[He's not buying it]

94
00:04:48,225 --> 00:04:49,708
[Kkakk Unni makes another offer]
Or, how about this?

95
00:04:49,708 --> 00:04:51,421
We're at the factory now.

96
00:04:51,421 --> 00:04:53,916
I will work here unpaid today.

97
00:04:53,916 --> 00:04:55,047
[Unpaid?]

98
00:04:55,047 --> 00:04:56,341
My employees, too.

99
00:04:56,341 --> 00:04:57,585
We'll work here.

100
00:04:57,585 --> 00:05:01,422
We could do, maybe, a ton?
We could produce a ton.

101
00:05:01,422 --> 00:05:03,025
Do you think you can pull that off?

102
00:05:03,025 --> 00:05:04,166
Yes, we could give it a try.

103
00:05:04,166 --> 00:05:09,684
If you do join us today with your employees,

104
00:05:09,684 --> 00:05:12,559
we'll go big and give it to you at *** won.

105
00:05:12,559 --> 00:05:14,094
[39% off their main product]
*** won for 2 servings of Kimchi Udon?

106
00:05:14,094 --> 00:05:15,599
- Yes.
- You promised me.

107
00:05:15,599 --> 00:05:18,314
- I promise you.
- Then, let's go get to work.

108
00:05:18,314 --> 00:05:19,724
I came all the way here.

109
00:05:19,724 --> 00:05:26,236
If I can trade my labor for a discount,
I would gladly do it. Of course.

110
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,534
[Before entering the factory]
Roll it on the front.

111
00:05:28,534 --> 00:05:32,201
[Going through strict hygiene control]
Wash thoroughly between your fingers.

112
00:05:32,892 --> 00:05:34,609
[Finally at the production line]
Whoa.

113
00:05:34,609 --> 00:05:36,283
Hello.

114
00:05:36,283 --> 00:05:38,748
[Hygiene and safety protocols were
strictly followed during filming]

115
00:05:38,748 --> 00:05:40,791
That's how you make skewers.

116
00:05:40,791 --> 00:05:43,272
[A factory running on free labor]

117
00:05:43,272 --> 00:05:45,556
- Spread this out.
- Yes.

118
00:05:45,556 --> 00:05:46,972
[Butchering manually]

119
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:49,923
- Are these all cut by hand, one by one?
- Yes.

120
00:05:49,923 --> 00:05:53,336
We cut them one by one
and skewer them manually.

121
00:05:53,336 --> 00:05:55,510
I'm so shocked.

122
00:05:55,510 --> 00:05:58,423
[Kkakk Unni sits at the workstation]

123
00:05:58,423 --> 00:06:00,526
- The meat has a grain.
- Oh, it has a grain.

124
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:02,822
Skewer it this way or this way.

125
00:06:02,822 --> 00:06:04,891
You have to skewer it along the grain,
not randomly.

126
00:06:04,891 --> 00:06:06,659
- I thought I could do it any way.
- No.

127
00:06:06,659 --> 00:06:09,005
This is no joke.

128
00:06:09,005 --> 00:06:11,548
You have to put in a lot of strength.

129
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:15,322
You need to speed up.
You're taking too long to finish.

130
00:06:15,322 --> 00:06:17,668
[Kkakk Unni is rushed by scolding]
I'll try to be faster.

131
00:06:17,668 --> 00:06:18,693
Wait.

132
00:06:18,693 --> 00:06:20,721
The bottom one...

133
00:06:20,721 --> 00:06:22,940
- Chicken.
- You work with your hands, not your mouth.

134
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:25,239
- I told you to speed up.
- Please bear with me.

135
00:06:25,239 --> 00:06:27,128
[A regrettable slip of the tongue]
I will work here unpaid today.

136
00:06:27,128 --> 00:06:29,558
We could produce a ton.

137
00:06:29,558 --> 00:06:35,674
Now I understand why the director didn't
give me a discount. This is a lot of hard work.

138
00:06:35,674 --> 00:06:37,140
It's impossible to think of anything else.

139
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:39,287
You have to skewer them precisely.

140
00:06:39,287 --> 00:06:41,558
You have to check them meticulously.

141
00:06:41,558 --> 00:06:44,464
It was surprisingly labor-intensive.

142
00:06:44,464 --> 00:06:47,217
[Filming content without fail]
You're working very hard.

143
00:06:47,217 --> 00:06:48,471
Take a look.

144
00:06:48,471 --> 00:06:49,859
I just made this one.

145
00:06:49,859 --> 00:06:51,345
Let me take a look.

146
00:06:52,759 --> 00:06:54,390
I'm so proud of myself.

147
00:06:54,390 --> 00:06:56,874
[Kkakk Unni does her best despite being tired]
I'm telling you, not everyone can do this.

148
00:06:56,874 --> 00:06:58,034
It's so much work.

149
00:06:58,034 --> 00:06:59,536
Show us.

150
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:02,525
If you're eating this skewer, please enjoy.

151
00:07:02,525 --> 00:07:05,373
[Negotiation to production, all done]
Alright, good.

152
00:07:06,344 --> 00:07:10,732
[Carefully prepared content goes live]

153
00:07:10,732 --> 00:07:11,744
Tudari's signature,

154
00:07:11,744 --> 00:07:15,731
assorted skewers and chicken wings
for Kkakk Unni's channel only.

155
00:07:16,372 --> 00:07:17,373
[Closed]

156
00:07:17,373 --> 00:07:22,129
[Selling out as soon as content goes live]

157
00:07:22,129 --> 00:07:24,403
I just want one thing.

158
00:07:24,403 --> 00:07:27,823
I want people to know
that I don't just sell anything.

159
00:07:27,823 --> 00:07:31,422
I want them to know I strive for a good deal

160
00:07:31,422 --> 00:07:34,317
and work hard to bring good products to them.

161
00:07:34,317 --> 00:07:35,618
That's all I want.

162
00:07:35,618 --> 00:07:37,693
[Will her sincere efforts pay off
after the fierce negotiation?]

163
00:07:37,693 --> 00:07:40,699
[Packing something here, too]

164
00:07:40,699 --> 00:07:42,299
[Packing with love]
Phew.

165
00:07:44,412 --> 00:07:46,534
Hello, I love you.

166
00:07:46,534 --> 00:07:47,813
That sounds lame.

167
00:07:47,813 --> 00:07:49,483
[Contemplating]

168
00:07:49,483 --> 00:07:53,720
If you're putting on Sangeununnie's lashes,
you're beautiful!

169
00:07:54,254 --> 00:07:57,831
Today, I'm going with "Sangeun Dash."

170
00:07:57,831 --> 00:08:00,180
I'm going to deliver false lashes.

171
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:04,150
These are false lashes developed
from my hands-on experience.

172
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:05,981
You can choose based on the mood
you're going for.

173
00:08:05,981 --> 00:08:07,206
[The first shipment is already out]
There are three types.

174
00:08:07,206 --> 00:08:11,441
I posted a form asking everyone who bought it
to submit proof of purchase.

175
00:08:11,441 --> 00:08:13,033
[Riding the momentum
with a proof-of-purchase event]

176
00:08:13,033 --> 00:08:14,338
[The reaction was explosive]

177
00:08:14,338 --> 00:08:16,156
[Buying right now! / I got them too /
Can't live without them / I ordered already!]

178
00:08:17,568 --> 00:08:21,989
I randomly selected some participants,
and I'll deliver the gifts to them in person.

179
00:08:21,989 --> 00:08:23,573
[Driving herself, too]

180
00:08:23,573 --> 00:08:25,173
Broom, broom.

181
00:08:26,441 --> 00:08:28,075
Let's get going.

182
00:08:28,075 --> 00:08:30,516
[On her way to meet her fans, Sanggomi]

183
00:08:32,466 --> 00:08:35,157
How do you feel about meeting Sanggomi?

184
00:08:35,157 --> 00:08:37,689
This is your first time meeting them in person.

185
00:08:37,689 --> 00:08:39,700
I'm a bit nervous.

186
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:45,867
It's not very common for me to meet Sanggomi.

187
00:08:45,867 --> 00:08:49,849
I have many Sanggomi customers,

188
00:08:49,849 --> 00:08:53,222
but it feels different from meeting them
at work.

189
00:08:53,222 --> 00:08:57,443
It feels even more special meeting them
outside work.

190
00:08:58,215 --> 00:09:00,165
They'll be able to recognize me, right?

191
00:09:00,165 --> 00:09:03,071
They may have already caught on over the phone.

192
00:09:03,071 --> 00:09:04,690
You sounded too you.

193
00:09:04,690 --> 00:09:05,933
I didn't!

194
00:09:05,933 --> 00:09:06,945
[A piercing look]

195
00:09:08,174 --> 00:09:09,776
What should I do?

196
00:09:09,776 --> 00:09:12,548
[Calling them before departure]

197
00:09:12,548 --> 00:09:13,549
<i>Hello?</i>

198
00:09:13,549 --> 00:09:15,081
Hello.

199
00:09:15,081 --> 00:09:16,506
[That's straight up Sangeununnie]
<i>Yes?</i>

200
00:09:16,506 --> 00:09:20,399
Am I speaking with ***, who won false lashes?

201
00:09:20,399 --> 00:09:21,400
Hello.

202
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:23,982
[Did Sanggomi catch on?]
Hello.

203
00:09:25,295 --> 00:09:28,912
[On the way to meet the first Sanggomi]
I have to show up looking perfect.

204
00:09:29,601 --> 00:09:32,148
[A disguise for the big moment]

205
00:09:32,148 --> 00:09:35,892
We're downstairs, could you please come down?

206
00:09:35,892 --> 00:09:36,893
<i>Yes.</i>

207
00:09:36,893 --> 00:09:39,169
[30 seconds before meeting Sanggomi]
Thank you.

208
00:09:40,138 --> 00:09:41,982
[Overexcited with anticipation]

209
00:09:45,107 --> 00:09:46,130
[Sanggomi appears]

210
00:09:46,901 --> 00:09:48,730
- Oh!
- Hello.

211
00:09:48,730 --> 00:09:50,230
Hello.

212
00:09:50,230 --> 00:09:51,990
[Finally meeting the first Sanggomi]

213
00:09:51,990 --> 00:09:53,590
- Oh!
- Hello.

214
00:09:55,449 --> 00:09:56,777
- Are you ***?
- I am.

215
00:09:56,777 --> 00:09:58,552
- I came to deliver this to you.
- Hello.

216
00:09:58,552 --> 00:10:00,127
How did you come here yourself?

217
00:10:00,127 --> 00:10:02,690
[Sanggomi recognized Sangeununnie right away]
Oh, you recognized me.

218
00:10:02,690 --> 00:10:07,715
Your voice on the phone sounded a little
like your work voice.

219
00:10:07,715 --> 00:10:09,440
- Really?
- Yes.

220
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:11,040
I wasn't sure, but...

221
00:10:11,702 --> 00:10:12,907
Hello.

222
00:10:12,907 --> 00:10:15,557
[Her identity revealed by her voice alone]
I thought I changed it just fine.

223
00:10:15,557 --> 00:10:16,844
I am Sanggomi.

224
00:10:16,844 --> 00:10:18,371
Thank you.

225
00:10:18,371 --> 00:10:19,372
Thank you.

226
00:10:19,372 --> 00:10:23,329
- I put them on today because I'm going out.
- Oh, you did.

227
00:10:23,329 --> 00:10:24,752
[Checking]
For later today.

228
00:10:24,752 --> 00:10:26,905
You did! You put them on so well.

229
00:10:26,905 --> 00:10:29,160
I practiced with your content on YouTube.

230
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:31,759
[Sanggomi learned from Sangeununnie's content]
Well done. Good job. I'm proud of you.

231
00:10:31,759 --> 00:10:34,751
What was your favorite thing so far?

232
00:10:34,751 --> 00:10:39,333
I liked Heart Percent and Gash.

233
00:10:39,333 --> 00:10:40,824
Oh, also that.

234
00:10:40,824 --> 00:10:42,918
[The purchase list is endless]
I feel like I bought too many.

235
00:10:42,918 --> 00:10:45,734
- I have *** too.
- Really? You bought almost everything.

236
00:10:45,734 --> 00:10:47,736
Thank you.

237
00:10:47,736 --> 00:10:50,161
Everything I bought didn't disappoint me.

238
00:10:50,161 --> 00:10:51,768
[Sangeununnie's recommendations can be trusted]
Never.

239
00:10:51,768 --> 00:10:52,914
Of course.

240
00:10:52,914 --> 00:10:56,418
There are two more rounds left.

241
00:10:56,418 --> 00:11:00,748
Is there anything that you want me to sell?

242
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:05,361
The thing is, you had already sold
almost every type of beauty product.

243
00:11:05,361 --> 00:11:06,912
- I did cover most of them.
- Yes.

244
00:11:06,912 --> 00:11:10,227
I think ingestible beauty products are popular
these days.

245
00:11:10,227 --> 00:11:14,024
- Something for bad breath sounds good, too.
- Bad breath. That's important.

246
00:11:14,024 --> 00:11:15,733
You also dress very nicely.

247
00:11:15,733 --> 00:11:16,734
[Spinning]

248
00:11:16,734 --> 00:11:22,583
I think clothing could be a fresh category.

249
00:11:22,583 --> 00:11:25,166
[Refreshing feedback]
I'll try to work on that. Thank you.

250
00:11:25,166 --> 00:11:26,409
Good luck.

251
00:11:26,409 --> 00:11:28,373
- Thank you.
- See you again.

252
00:11:28,373 --> 00:11:31,197
- You're so pretty.
- Thank you.

253
00:11:31,197 --> 00:11:34,990
[Getting a photo to remember the day]
First of all, she has a strong belief in me.

254
00:11:34,990 --> 00:11:39,280
It made me realize
that I really need to become an artist

255
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:42,249
and a seller who lives up to that trust.

256
00:11:42,249 --> 00:11:46,211
I loved getting so much energy
from my subscribers.

257
00:11:46,211 --> 00:11:47,239
I was touched.

258
00:11:47,239 --> 00:11:51,625
I drove a lot, and it was a bit tiring,

259
00:11:51,625 --> 00:11:54,933
but I got more energy from meeting them.

260
00:11:54,933 --> 00:11:56,215
[An experience where she gained a lot]
It was very nice.

261
00:11:56,215 --> 00:12:02,046
About 99% of my followers and Sanggomi
are women.

262
00:12:02,046 --> 00:12:04,980
But the last person I met was a guy.

263
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:07,543
[Before heading to the third destination]

264
00:12:07,543 --> 00:12:08,694
<i>Hello.</i>

265
00:12:08,694 --> 00:12:11,672
Hello, am I speaking with Kim **?

266
00:12:11,672 --> 00:12:12,673
<i>Speaking.</i>

267
00:12:12,673 --> 00:12:16,513
I'm calling to inform you you've won
the EyeMe false lashes purchase event.

268
00:12:16,513 --> 00:12:18,788
Would it be okay for us to visit you
at around 3:30?

269
00:12:18,788 --> 00:12:22,076
<i>Yes, I think I'll still be here.
That works for me.</i>

270
00:12:22,076 --> 00:12:25,070
[Sangeununnie on the phone with male Sanggomi]
Okay, thank you. I'll see you soon.

271
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:31,119
I was wondering what a man would use
false lashes for.

272
00:12:32,652 --> 00:12:34,500
[Still wearing a disguise]

273
00:12:35,345 --> 00:12:36,984
[Many strollers]

274
00:12:39,671 --> 00:12:42,242
[A front door with Chinese-style decor]

275
00:12:44,214 --> 00:12:45,814
[Ding-dong]

276
00:12:49,239 --> 00:12:51,680
[Nervous]

277
00:12:52,917 --> 00:12:54,621
Hello. Mr. Kim.

278
00:12:54,621 --> 00:12:56,289
You are Sangeununnie, aren't you?

279
00:12:56,289 --> 00:12:57,290
You are Sangeununnie, aren't you?

280
00:12:57,290 --> 00:12:58,352
[Will her identity be revealed again?]

281
00:12:58,352 --> 00:12:59,518
- No, I'm not.
- Honey.

282
00:12:59,518 --> 00:13:01,689
Honey.

283
00:13:01,689 --> 00:13:02,761
Honey.

284
00:13:02,761 --> 00:13:04,048
[The winner suddenly calls for his wife]

285
00:13:05,415 --> 00:13:06,556
What?

286
00:13:06,556 --> 00:13:07,557
Come in, come in.

287
00:13:07,557 --> 00:13:09,963
Hi, but why are you here?

288
00:13:10,858 --> 00:13:12,533
[It was Cui Shishi from Team China]

289
00:13:12,533 --> 00:13:13,534
What a surprise.

290
00:13:13,534 --> 00:13:15,621
- What are you doing here?
- Oh my gosh.

291
00:13:15,621 --> 00:13:16,701
[A warm greeting with a hug]

292
00:13:16,701 --> 00:13:18,239
Wow, this is incredible.

293
00:13:18,239 --> 00:13:19,414
I didn't see this coming.

294
00:13:19,414 --> 00:13:21,204
[The last Sanggomi was Cui Shishi's husband]
Wow, you have two kids.

295
00:13:21,204 --> 00:13:22,514
- May I come in?
- Of course.

296
00:13:22,514 --> 00:13:24,245
Thank you.

297
00:13:24,245 --> 00:13:27,219
I was so surprised to see Shishi.

298
00:13:27,219 --> 00:13:31,248
Even though we're rivals, she bought my lashes.

299
00:13:31,248 --> 00:13:33,201
She says she loves my false lashes.

300
00:13:33,201 --> 00:13:34,566
[What can I do?]

301
00:13:34,566 --> 00:13:38,998
My favorite influencer has great makeup skills.

302
00:13:38,998 --> 00:13:44,313
It was such a joy to have her at my home.

303
00:13:44,313 --> 00:13:48,979
You did buy my lashes. Thank you.

304
00:13:48,979 --> 00:13:52,291
Because we are rivals,
I need to see what my opponent is selling.

305
00:13:52,291 --> 00:13:54,716
I need to see it and study it.

306
00:13:54,716 --> 00:13:58,186
She wanted to check what other teams sold
and bought some as a reference,

307
00:13:58,186 --> 00:14:01,230
thinking she could sell them herself
if they looked promising.

308
00:14:01,230 --> 00:14:02,370
[Cui Shishi has a different mindset]

309
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:04,795
You do think differently.

310
00:14:04,795 --> 00:14:07,292
There's a saying in China that goes

311
00:14:07,292 --> 00:14:10,260
"Know your enemy, know yourself,
and you need not fear a hundred battles."

312
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:13,829
So I keep an eye on what others are selling
and buy them myself.

313
00:14:13,829 --> 00:14:17,270
[Buying and trying the rival team's products
to improve]

314
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:19,884
I bought it, but I'm not familiar
with how to use it.

315
00:14:19,884 --> 00:14:23,319
I'll have to watch your video and learn.

316
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,645
Do you want me to put the lashes on you?

317
00:14:25,645 --> 00:14:26,942
I can do it for you.

318
00:14:26,942 --> 00:14:29,542
[Live demonstration since she's already here]

319
00:14:31,889 --> 00:14:34,526
Oh, this is your kitchen.

320
00:14:34,526 --> 00:14:37,289
Let me see where I put the tweezers.

321
00:14:37,289 --> 00:14:40,662
[What surprised Sangeununnie?]
Wow.

322
00:14:40,662 --> 00:14:42,765
[Cabinets full of cosmetics]

323
00:14:42,765 --> 00:14:46,171
You got bigger cabinets than the ones
in my studio.

324
00:14:46,171 --> 00:14:48,614
I have a lot of samples I use
on my livestreams.

325
00:14:48,614 --> 00:14:51,024
[A lot of K-beauty products]
D'Alba and everything.

326
00:14:51,024 --> 00:14:52,509
And there's this.

327
00:14:52,509 --> 00:14:54,217
[There are more]

328
00:14:54,217 --> 00:14:56,321
You've got everything from lotions to gowns.

329
00:14:56,321 --> 00:14:57,517
Does this work?

330
00:14:57,517 --> 00:14:59,017
It does.

331
00:14:59,017 --> 00:15:01,992
[Shishi's trolley cart full of cosmetics]
So you keep them like this.

332
00:15:01,992 --> 00:15:04,398
There's a reason her skin is so fair.

333
00:15:05,922 --> 00:15:07,716
Shall we start, then?

334
00:15:08,210 --> 00:15:10,521
[Time to put the false lashes on]

335
00:15:11,345 --> 00:15:15,351
There are a variety of designs.

336
00:15:15,351 --> 00:15:19,732
Let's try the most popular ones
that give a clean look.

337
00:15:20,870 --> 00:15:24,788
There are separate under lashes.

338
00:15:27,536 --> 00:15:28,751
Put them on the tweezers like this.

339
00:15:28,751 --> 00:15:30,077
[Sangeununnie teaches how to use false lashes]

340
00:15:30,077 --> 00:15:33,443
I think you can just put them
on your natural lashes.

341
00:15:34,391 --> 00:15:38,500
Your eyelashes are thin, so they stick easily.

342
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:43,555
These lashes feel natural like your own,
so they sell well in Korea.

343
00:15:44,172 --> 00:15:46,691
Your eyes are so pretty, teacher.

344
00:15:46,691 --> 00:15:49,126
Thank you. I can do the same makeup for you.

345
00:15:49,126 --> 00:15:50,469
- You will?
- Of course.

346
00:15:50,469 --> 00:15:52,339
Should we schedule it?

347
00:15:52,339 --> 00:15:56,631
I can invite Team China's members
to visit and learn from you.

348
00:15:56,631 --> 00:15:58,504
Oh, sounds like a good idea.

349
00:15:58,504 --> 00:16:01,434
[Makeup lecture is set up with Team China]
I am a great teacher.

350
00:16:01,434 --> 00:16:03,782
These look so natural.

351
00:16:03,782 --> 00:16:05,325
They do.

352
00:16:05,325 --> 00:16:06,832
[Happy]
Great. I like them.

353
00:16:06,832 --> 00:16:07,833
Nice.

354
00:16:07,833 --> 00:16:10,353
My eyelashes look much fuller now.

355
00:16:10,353 --> 00:16:11,354
My eyes.

356
00:16:11,354 --> 00:16:13,173
They look bigger.

357
00:16:13,173 --> 00:16:14,871
[Her eyes are naturally defined]
They look bigger, but in a natural way.

358
00:16:14,871 --> 00:16:16,490
Right.

359
00:16:16,490 --> 00:16:18,090
Good.

360
00:16:18,592 --> 00:16:21,931
I met many customers today.

361
00:16:21,931 --> 00:16:23,985
I appreciate all of them.

362
00:16:23,985 --> 00:16:29,236
These customers watched my content
and bought the products.

363
00:16:29,236 --> 00:16:31,665
It meant a lot to me.

364
00:16:31,665 --> 00:16:34,868
I'll keep working hard
and do my best going forward.

365
00:16:35,558 --> 00:16:37,591
[Round 3 has not finished yet]
Skincare with your hands when there's this?

366
00:16:37,591 --> 00:16:38,919
Gua Sha that stretches your skin?

367
00:16:38,919 --> 00:16:40,538
[Sangeununnie picked a high-ticket item]

368
00:16:40,538 --> 00:16:42,138
<i>Air-shot mode.</i>

369
00:16:43,406 --> 00:16:48,991
[Team Korea's full sprint toward first place]

370
00:16:49,731 --> 00:16:52,432
[Singapore]

371
00:16:52,432 --> 00:16:54,780
[Team SG & MY gathered for an urgent meeting]

372
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:57,713
We're fine. Surviving.

373
00:16:59,023 --> 00:17:01,602
[The two in Malaysia joined on a video call]

374
00:17:01,602 --> 00:17:05,116
I think we need to start planning for Round 3.

375
00:17:05,116 --> 00:17:09,182
We were in fifth place in Round 2.

376
00:17:09,182 --> 00:17:11,045
Yes, we were.

377
00:17:11,045 --> 00:17:14,216
That was a significant fall.

378
00:17:14,216 --> 00:17:16,911
Fifth place goes to Team Singapore & Malaysia.

379
00:17:16,911 --> 00:17:19,564
[Fell from third to fifth place]

380
00:17:19,564 --> 00:17:22,141
I don't want it, I don't want it.

381
00:17:22,141 --> 00:17:26,454
[A stunned look at the unexpected results]

382
00:17:26,454 --> 00:17:29,633
Honestly, I was pretty shocked
that we ended up in fifth place,

383
00:17:29,633 --> 00:17:32,965
considering we were in third place in Round 1.

384
00:17:32,965 --> 00:17:39,046
But at the same time, I knew we had exhausted
all our efforts in Round 1.

385
00:17:39,046 --> 00:17:41,915
So, naturally,
we showed a lackluster performance in Round 2.

386
00:17:41,915 --> 00:17:43,218
[Their total sales in Round 2 halved
from Round 1]

387
00:17:43,218 --> 00:17:44,928
Yeah.

388
00:17:44,928 --> 00:17:45,929
[1.4 billion won gap]

389
00:17:45,929 --> 00:17:48,139
[Their total sales in Round 2 were
less than half of Round 1's]

390
00:17:50,551 --> 00:17:53,631
In Round 2,
I think we were all tired from Round 1.

391
00:17:53,631 --> 00:17:55,655
We pushed too hard in Round 1.

392
00:17:55,655 --> 00:17:57,810
- Yeah.
- So Round 2 was hard.

393
00:17:57,810 --> 00:18:00,836
There's this particular mission in Round 3,
Limit Break.

394
00:18:00,836 --> 00:18:02,413
Yes.

395
00:18:02,413 --> 00:18:03,902
We didn't do well in Round 2.

396
00:18:03,902 --> 00:18:06,795
And it just so happens that the Round 3 mission
has a special challenge

397
00:18:06,795 --> 00:18:09,936
where we have to beat our Round 2 sales.

398
00:18:09,936 --> 00:18:11,770
I don't think it'll be too difficult.

399
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:14,187
Part of the rule is
that we have to push our limits.

400
00:18:14,187 --> 00:18:15,777
[Poor Round 2 sales turn into an opportunity]
I don't think that'll be too difficult.

401
00:18:15,777 --> 00:18:18,439
This is a good chance to catch up.

402
00:18:18,439 --> 00:18:21,843
It's a blessing in disguise
that we didn't do well.

403
00:18:21,843 --> 00:18:22,865
- Exactly.
- True.

404
00:18:22,865 --> 00:18:24,528
[Turning crisis into opportunity]
It's all part of the plan.

405
00:18:24,528 --> 00:18:25,756
Maybe it was all part of a plan.

406
00:18:25,756 --> 00:18:26,968
Everything happens for a reason.

407
00:18:26,968 --> 00:18:28,509
- Yeah.
- Yes.

408
00:18:28,509 --> 00:18:31,584
[Malaysia]

409
00:18:31,584 --> 00:18:34,786
[Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia]

410
00:18:35,587 --> 00:18:37,146
[Neat, spacious office]

411
00:18:37,902 --> 00:18:40,224
[Canteen for employee welfare]

412
00:18:40,224 --> 00:18:42,263
[Numerous award plaques]

413
00:18:43,013 --> 00:18:44,888
[A large studio for livestreaming]

414
00:18:45,417 --> 00:18:49,599
[Plus mini studios for solo livestreams]

415
00:18:53,314 --> 00:18:57,935
[What is this place
with a well-organized system?]

416
00:18:59,585 --> 00:19:01,984
[Today's star arrives at the office]

417
00:19:01,984 --> 00:19:03,075
[Elle Onni, premium brand power seller]

418
00:19:03,075 --> 00:19:05,472
Hello, everyone. I'm here.

419
00:19:05,472 --> 00:19:06,903
Hello.

420
00:19:06,903 --> 00:19:11,609
Jing Yu, do we have a new poster
for X THE LEAGUE?

421
00:19:11,609 --> 00:19:14,139
Can you send it to me later?

422
00:19:15,374 --> 00:19:17,475
Hello, I'm Elle Onni.

423
00:19:17,475 --> 00:19:22,081
I'm a member of Team Singapore and Malaysia.

424
00:19:22,081 --> 00:19:26,068
I'm the founder of Onni Mart
and a livestreamer.

425
00:19:28,234 --> 00:19:34,263
[Elle Onni's livestream commerce channel]

426
00:19:35,078 --> 00:19:38,442
[Live selling is the basics]

427
00:19:39,037 --> 00:19:41,269
[Various commerce content is a plus]

428
00:19:41,269 --> 00:19:43,398
I call my store in Malaysia "Onni Mart"

429
00:19:43,398 --> 00:19:50,336
because I am like an "onni"
(sister in Korean) to my followers.

430
00:19:50,336 --> 00:19:53,788
That's why everyone calls me "Elle Onni."

431
00:19:53,788 --> 00:19:56,661
I loved visiting Korea.

432
00:19:56,661 --> 00:19:59,254
I also did proxy buying for Korean products.

433
00:19:59,254 --> 00:20:04,224
[A pioneer who brought Korean products
to Malaysia]

434
00:20:05,226 --> 00:20:09,758
[Even standing shoulder to shoulder
with actress Lee Young Ae]

435
00:20:09,758 --> 00:20:16,916
I also achieved a million-ringgit sales record
in just six minutes.

436
00:20:18,876 --> 00:20:22,368
[340 million Korean won in sales
just in six minutes of livestreaming]

437
00:20:22,368 --> 00:20:25,579
She sold a million ringgit in six minutes.

438
00:20:25,579 --> 00:20:29,013
A million ringgit
in just six minutes is amazing.

439
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,864
Six minutes.

440
00:20:30,864 --> 00:20:32,645
Will we be okay?

441
00:20:32,645 --> 00:20:35,266
[Malaysian power seller Elle Onni
surprises everyone]

442
00:20:35,266 --> 00:20:37,802
[Another strength that stands out
in Elle Onni's career]

443
00:20:38,455 --> 00:20:44,255
There are awards that meant a lot to me
in my life.

444
00:20:44,255 --> 00:20:49,653
[Three-time top seller award winner]

445
00:20:51,521 --> 00:20:56,840
[How will Elle Onni's performance
impact the team?]

446
00:20:56,840 --> 00:21:00,812
[An unexpected twist amid the anticipation]

447
00:21:00,812 --> 00:21:04,446
One of our team members, Elle Onni, is
going through a personal matter.

448
00:21:04,446 --> 00:21:07,703
[An unexpected problem hit Team SG & MY]
Elle Onni...

449
00:21:07,703 --> 00:21:09,183
I hope she gets better.

450
00:21:09,183 --> 00:21:13,676
As soon as she arrived in Korea
a couple of days ago,

451
00:21:13,676 --> 00:21:17,022
she had to leave immediately.

452
00:21:17,022 --> 00:21:20,729
[Elle Onni couldn't be there
for the Round 3 pre-mission]

453
00:21:20,729 --> 00:21:22,513
No, no.

454
00:21:24,338 --> 00:21:28,247
[What happened to Elle Onni?]
Hello.

455
00:21:29,110 --> 00:21:34,273
During our last beauty product sale,
I was hospitalized.

456
00:21:34,273 --> 00:21:37,654
So I wasn't able to do livestreaming.

457
00:21:37,654 --> 00:21:39,789
[While everyone kept selling hard in Round 1]

458
00:21:39,789 --> 00:21:42,810
[Elle Onni's sales remained low]

459
00:21:43,326 --> 00:21:46,456
[Elle Onni struggled in Rounds 1 and 2]

460
00:21:46,456 --> 00:21:54,895
When I returned to Malaysia
after filming Round 1 in Korea,

461
00:21:54,895 --> 00:21:58,349
I went to get a health checkup.

462
00:21:58,349 --> 00:22:00,949
And I found out I had breast cancer.

463
00:22:02,604 --> 00:22:08,376
[A breast cancer diagnosis brought life
to a halt]

464
00:22:09,588 --> 00:22:15,232
After talking to my doctor,
I had to start treatment right away.

465
00:22:16,070 --> 00:22:20,207
It only took three days to get surgery
after the checkup.

466
00:22:20,207 --> 00:22:26,532
[A bilateral mastectomy just three days
after diagnosis]

467
00:22:30,917 --> 00:22:35,782
[Treatment began
before she could have a second thought]

468
00:22:37,456 --> 00:22:41,642
[Elle Onni told her three daughters
about her condition]

469
00:22:41,642 --> 00:22:47,160
All three of my children were breastfed.

470
00:22:51,659 --> 00:22:57,022
I told my kids,
"Your mom's breasts are retired now."

471
00:22:57,022 --> 00:22:58,482
My kids are great at comforting me.

472
00:22:58,482 --> 00:23:01,469
They told me I am prettier now.

473
00:23:01,469 --> 00:23:03,094
They came to hug me.

474
00:23:03,094 --> 00:23:06,787
They told me I'll get better soon.

475
00:23:10,081 --> 00:23:13,532
The whole process was okay.

476
00:23:13,532 --> 00:23:17,813
I wasn't too sad thanks to my children.

477
00:23:18,675 --> 00:23:23,720
[Elle Onni, overcoming her pain
with the love of her three daughters]

478
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:26,823
That's how I recovered from breast cancer.

479
00:23:26,823 --> 00:23:31,738
Now I can return to X THE LEAGUE.

480
00:23:31,738 --> 00:23:32,739
But...

481
00:23:32,739 --> 00:23:37,397
Round 3 of X THE LEAGUE, the international
commerce competition, is now underway.

482
00:23:37,397 --> 00:23:38,407
[Round 3 began]
Yes.

483
00:23:38,407 --> 00:23:42,227
[But Elle Onni couldn't participate
in the shoot]

484
00:23:42,916 --> 00:23:51,348
As soon as I landed in Korea,

485
00:23:51,348 --> 00:23:55,226
I received a video from my family.

486
00:23:55,226 --> 00:23:59,598
They said my father's condition had
suddenly become critical.

487
00:23:59,598 --> 00:24:04,776
[News of her father's worsening condition
during a difficult time]

488
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:11,241
[Her father suffered a stroke 14 years ago]

489
00:24:12,223 --> 00:24:14,283
I didn't want it to affect my teammates.

490
00:24:14,283 --> 00:24:16,929
It could have been the last moment
of my father's life.

491
00:24:16,929 --> 00:24:19,372
I was afraid he might pass away like that,
so I eventually went back home.

