994
00:50:45,591 --> 00:50:48,362
so they probably won't get many bonus points.

995
00:50:48,362 --> 00:50:54,265
We might even pass the USA and Vietnam.

996
00:50:55,487 --> 00:50:58,959
[Lower-ranked teams grow nervous
after the total sales ranking]

997
00:50:59,904 --> 00:51:05,834
[Can mission points help
the lower-ranked teams make a comeback?]

998
00:51:06,377 --> 00:51:07,387
[Round 3 Limit Break]

999
00:51:07,387 --> 00:51:10,181
We'll now announce the Round 3 results.

1000
00:51:11,749 --> 00:51:14,985
Starting with the X3 Platinum tier.

1001
00:51:15,820 --> 00:51:17,221
Eighth place,

1002
00:51:18,055 --> 00:51:19,557
Japan,

1003
00:51:20,625 --> 00:51:22,693
with 47 points.

1004
00:51:22,693 --> 00:51:25,530
[Sales 15, Mission 28, Pop-up 4]

1005
00:51:25,530 --> 00:51:29,078
Our Round 3 sales are 500 times

1006
00:51:29,078 --> 00:51:30,968
[Fact: about 50 times]
our Round 2 sales.

1007
00:51:31,936 --> 00:51:34,538
[Sales are much higher
than the previous round, but...]

1008
00:51:35,276 --> 00:51:40,511
[Low total sales keep Japan from climbing back]

1009
00:51:40,511 --> 00:51:43,815
Sales were higher than Round 2, but...

1010
00:51:43,815 --> 00:51:46,884
[Disappointing total sales]
The total sales weren't that high.

1011
00:51:46,884 --> 00:51:49,720
[7th in the pre-mission Pop-up Rush]
And their pre-mission score was low too.

1012
00:51:51,421 --> 00:51:52,857
Seventh place,

1013
00:51:53,995 --> 00:51:55,392
the USA,

1014
00:51:56,561 --> 00:51:58,663
with 54 points.

1015
00:51:58,663 --> 00:52:00,302
[Sales 25, Mission 24, Pop-up 5]

1016
00:52:01,132 --> 00:52:03,487
The USA is seventh.

1017
00:52:03,487 --> 00:52:05,369
Then who's sixth?

1018
00:52:06,554 --> 00:52:09,246
- The USA actually dropped.
- They were sixth.

1019
00:52:09,246 --> 00:52:10,454
- They dropped.
- Exactly.

1020
00:52:10,454 --> 00:52:13,788
Now I'm worried about us.

1021
00:52:13,788 --> 00:52:15,354
[Nervous]

1022
00:52:15,354 --> 00:52:16,847
Sixth place,

1023
00:52:18,953 --> 00:52:20,384
Vietnam.

1024
00:52:21,120 --> 00:52:24,154
[Sales 30, Mission 24, Pop-up 3]
A total of 57 points.

1025
00:52:24,755 --> 00:52:27,124
[Three countries land
in the X3 tier in Round 3]

1026
00:52:27,124 --> 00:52:29,820
[Vietnam drops from 3rd to 6th]

1027
00:52:29,820 --> 00:52:33,598
So we ended up dropping in the rankings.

1028
00:52:33,598 --> 00:52:36,321
We were third in Round 2,

1029
00:52:36,321 --> 00:52:40,070
and now we've fallen all the way to sixth.
It's practically the bottom.

1030
00:52:40,605 --> 00:52:44,208
I'm not even one percent satisfied with myself.

1031
00:52:47,612 --> 00:52:50,381
[Round 3 leaves only regret and disappointment]

1032
00:52:50,381 --> 00:52:51,949
I'm really upset.

1033
00:52:51,949 --> 00:52:55,070
[Silence after the shocking drop in ranking]

1034
00:52:55,654 --> 00:52:58,321
- Vietnam?
- Vietnam dropped in the rankings.

1035
00:52:58,321 --> 00:53:00,220
Then Thailand must've moved up.

1036
00:53:00,220 --> 00:53:02,026
Yes! We passed Vietnam!

1037
00:53:05,299 --> 00:53:08,365
Are we fifth?

1038
00:53:09,020 --> 00:53:12,169
Now for the X2 Emerald tier.

1039
00:53:12,637 --> 00:53:16,974
Fifth place, Thailand.

1040
00:53:18,843 --> 00:53:21,812
[Sales 20, Mission 32, Pop-up 6]
A total of 58 points.

1041
00:53:22,280 --> 00:53:25,655
[Team Thailand rebounds from 7th to 5th]

1042
00:53:26,350 --> 00:53:28,286
[Crown pose]

1043
00:53:28,286 --> 00:53:32,189
Everyone, Thailand moved up to fifth!

1044
00:53:33,424 --> 00:53:35,754
[Thrilled]

1045
00:53:35,754 --> 00:53:39,230
Thailand moved up to the X2 tier.

1046
00:53:39,230 --> 00:53:40,898
We were seventh in total sales at first.

1047
00:53:40,898 --> 00:53:43,234
Now we're fifth. Oh, my gosh.

1048
00:53:43,234 --> 00:53:46,220
[Team Thailand enters the X2 tier
for the first time]

1049
00:53:46,220 --> 00:53:48,873
[5th Thailand: 58, 6th Vietnam: 57]

1050
00:53:48,873 --> 00:53:51,679
[Just one point separates 5th and 6th]
[So close]

1051
00:53:51,679 --> 00:53:53,110
Fourth place,

1052
00:53:54,345 --> 00:53:55,980
Korea,

1053
00:53:56,951 --> 00:53:59,717
with 66 points.

1054
00:53:59,717 --> 00:54:01,528
[Sales 35, Mission 24, Pop-up 7]

1055
00:54:03,321 --> 00:54:05,856
[Team Korea drops to X2 after finishing 4th]

1056
00:54:05,856 --> 00:54:07,425
Oh, my gosh.

1057
00:54:07,425 --> 00:54:12,763
We worked so hard,
but the sales just weren't enough.

1058
00:54:16,968 --> 00:54:21,038
[Only three countries remain]

1059
00:54:21,672 --> 00:54:23,073
Third place.

1060
00:54:25,209 --> 00:54:27,120
We got nine points in the pre-mission.

1061
00:54:27,120 --> 00:54:29,083
We have our pre-mission points too.

1062
00:54:29,083 --> 00:54:34,023
[Which of the three teams takes 3rd
in the final Round 3 ranking?]

1063
00:54:34,621 --> 00:54:37,588
Third place, China.

1064
00:54:39,457 --> 00:54:41,920
[Sales 45, Mission 24, Pop-up 10]
A total of 79 points.

1065
00:54:41,920 --> 00:54:45,630
[China drops from 2nd in total sales
to 3rd overall]

1066
00:54:45,630 --> 00:54:47,832
[Shocked]

1067
00:54:47,832 --> 00:54:50,768
That's why mission points are so important.

1068
00:54:50,768 --> 00:54:54,254
It's such a shame
we didn't earn more mission points.

1069
00:54:54,254 --> 00:54:56,807
[Team SG&MY automatically locks in X1]
Oh, my gosh.

1070
00:54:56,807 --> 00:54:59,243
I think we're X1!

1071
00:54:59,243 --> 00:55:01,646
[We finally made X1 too]
We're X1!

1072
00:55:01,646 --> 00:55:03,581
Yes, guys.

1073
00:55:03,581 --> 00:55:06,884
Everyone, what place do you think
Indonesia got?

1074
00:55:06,884 --> 00:55:09,021
Wouldn't Indonesia be first?

1075
00:55:12,187 --> 00:55:15,396
Now for the X1 Diamond tier.

1076
00:55:15,396 --> 00:55:16,460
First place...

1077
00:55:16,460 --> 00:55:22,866
[Who takes 1st place in Round 3?]

1078
00:55:25,806 --> 00:55:27,638
First place,

1079
00:55:27,638 --> 00:55:29,206
Indonesia,

1080
00:55:30,007 --> 00:55:32,510
with 98 points.

1081
00:55:32,510 --> 00:55:34,812
[Sales 50, Mission 40, Pop-up 8]

1082
00:55:34,812 --> 00:55:39,154
[Indonesia takes 1st place overall in Round 3]

1083
00:55:39,154 --> 00:55:41,354
Indonesia won!

1084
00:55:41,354 --> 00:55:42,653
Oh, my gosh.

1085
00:55:42,653 --> 00:55:45,322
Go, Indonesia!

1086
00:55:45,322 --> 00:55:47,525
[Celebrating the victory with family]

1087
00:55:47,525 --> 00:55:50,187
We won!

1088
00:55:50,187 --> 00:55:53,630
Everyone, Indonesia won again.

1089
00:55:54,788 --> 00:55:58,002
I hope we can take first place in everything.

1090
00:55:58,002 --> 00:56:01,472
Second place, Singapore and Malaysia,

1091
00:56:02,721 --> 00:56:04,975
with 85 points.

1092
00:56:04,975 --> 00:56:07,164
[Sales 40, Mission 36, Pop-up 9]

1093
00:56:07,887 --> 00:56:09,987
[Team SG&MY finishes 2nd overall in Round 3]

1094
00:56:09,987 --> 00:56:11,654
Everyone, this is our first X1!

1095
00:56:11,654 --> 00:56:14,918
We went from fifth to second.

1096
00:56:16,688 --> 00:56:19,623
Great job. Everyone worked so hard.

1097
00:56:20,291 --> 00:56:21,759
Amazing.

1098
00:56:21,759 --> 00:56:23,998
This is our first time in X1.

1099
00:56:23,998 --> 00:56:26,463
This is great,
but I feel like I'm going to cry.

1100
00:56:27,665 --> 00:56:30,016
[Getting emotional]

1101
00:56:30,721 --> 00:56:34,505
To all our sellers, great work in Round 3.

1102
00:56:34,505 --> 00:56:37,975
X THE LEAGUE only gets tougher
and more competitive.

1103
00:56:37,975 --> 00:56:40,277
We'll see you in the next round.

1104
00:56:41,645 --> 00:56:46,851
Maybe it's actually a good thing
we didn't do so well in the earlier rounds.

1105
00:56:46,851 --> 00:56:51,055
[Mission points lift them from 3rd
in total sales to 2nd overall]

1106
00:56:51,055 --> 00:56:53,624
[Team Korea drops from 2nd
in Round 2 to 4th in Round 3]

1107
00:56:53,624 --> 00:56:56,326
Indonesia's going to be tough.

1108
00:56:58,162 --> 00:56:59,254
But they're impressive.

1109
00:56:59,254 --> 00:57:01,298
I have to give them credit.

1110
00:57:01,298 --> 00:57:03,233
They completely beat their own sales record.

1111
00:57:04,154 --> 00:57:09,340
Honestly, we've just been working hard
without any real strategy.

1112
00:57:09,340 --> 00:57:12,176
- Right.
- But seeing the results keep coming in,

1113
00:57:12,176 --> 00:57:14,979
- I think we need a strategy now.
- Right.

1114
00:57:14,979 --> 00:57:17,548
It's not just about sales.

1115
00:57:17,548 --> 00:57:20,987
How you do on the missions
really changes the rankings.

1116
00:57:20,987 --> 00:57:23,391
[Mission points push Team China down to X2]
China had high sales too, but...

1117
00:57:23,391 --> 00:57:25,526
- They dropped by missing the mission target.
- Right.

1118
00:57:25,526 --> 00:57:28,587
Thailand moved up thanks to its mission score,

1119
00:57:28,587 --> 00:57:31,695
while Vietnam dropped
because of its mission score.

1120
00:57:31,695 --> 00:57:33,531
We've got a shot too.

1121
00:57:33,531 --> 00:57:35,874
[Mission points: the deciding factor]
The missions are important.

1122
00:57:35,874 --> 00:57:40,241
What if we focus on the mission in Round 4

1123
00:57:40,241 --> 00:57:43,273
- and climb back up?
- Sounds good.

1124
00:57:44,742 --> 00:57:47,471
[What Round 4 mission will
change the teams' fate?]

1125
00:57:52,483 --> 00:57:55,186
Hello! I'm Tiffany Young, your host

1126
00:57:55,186 --> 00:57:57,188
for the international commerce competition,
X THE LEAGUE.

1127
00:57:57,188 --> 00:57:58,823
And I'm BamBam.

1128
00:57:58,823 --> 00:58:00,691
[Round 3 X3 Vietnam]

1129
00:58:00,691 --> 00:58:02,560
[Round 3 X2 Korea]

1130
00:58:02,560 --> 00:58:04,094
[Round 3 X1 Singapore & Malaysia]

1131
00:58:04,094 --> 00:58:07,097
Through this fierce selling competition,

1132
00:58:07,097 --> 00:58:09,099
[Round 3 X1 Indonesia]
you've had to fight to protect your team's tier

1133
00:58:09,099 --> 00:58:10,734
[Round 3 X3 Japan]
or move up

1134
00:58:10,734 --> 00:58:12,903
[Round 3 X2 Thailand]
to an even higher one,

1135
00:58:12,903 --> 00:58:14,342
[Round 3 X3 USA]
without letting your guard down

1136
00:58:14,342 --> 00:58:15,976
[Round 3 X2 China]
for even a moment.

1137
00:58:15,976 --> 00:58:18,776
And after this fierce journey,

1138
00:58:18,776 --> 00:58:24,081
X THE LEAGUE now has just two rounds left.

1139
00:58:24,654 --> 00:58:28,452
[Only two chances left
to turn the rankings around]

1140
00:58:28,452 --> 00:58:29,523
We're halfway there now.

1141
00:58:29,523 --> 00:58:31,354
So there's only one left.

1142
00:58:31,354 --> 00:58:32,953
Oh, no. Two left.

1143
00:58:32,953 --> 00:58:36,993
Nine countries, eight teams,
all chasing the same goal.

1144
00:58:36,993 --> 00:58:39,330
[Round 1 Pre-Mission: The First Pitch]
Through unpredictable missions

1145
00:58:39,330 --> 00:58:40,698
[Round 1 Ranking Battle]
and constantly shifting

1146
00:58:40,698 --> 00:58:41,765
[Round 2 Wild Card]
rankings,

1147
00:58:41,765 --> 00:58:42,967
[Round 3 Pre-Mission: Pop-up Rush]
each seller's sales

1148
00:58:42,967 --> 00:58:45,035
[Round 3 Limit Break]
determine the team's tier.

1149
00:58:45,035 --> 00:58:49,373
In this league, one person's performance
can lift the whole team,

1150
00:58:49,373 --> 00:58:53,444
while one bad result can
bring the entire team down.

1151
00:58:53,444 --> 00:58:55,880
Round 4, starting now,

1152
00:58:55,880 --> 00:58:59,850
will be tougher and more competitive than ever.

1153
00:59:00,551 --> 00:59:03,620
From here on, no one can survive alone.

1154
00:59:05,289 --> 00:59:07,558
[Can't survive alone?]

1155
00:59:07,558 --> 00:59:12,162
Will you survive together,
or fall apart on your own?

1156
00:59:14,365 --> 00:59:20,905
X THE LEAGUE Round 4 mission is Unity Or Fall.

1157
00:59:20,905 --> 00:59:24,642
[Unity Or Fall]

1158
00:59:24,642 --> 00:59:26,521
Unity Or Fall.

1159
00:59:26,521 --> 00:59:28,378
So it's basically a team mission.

1160
00:59:29,020 --> 00:59:30,947
You need at least two people.

1161
00:59:32,116 --> 00:59:33,951
Unity Or Fall.

1162
00:59:33,951 --> 00:59:36,787
Here are the rules for Unity Or Fall.

1163
00:59:36,787 --> 00:59:38,923
During the round, sellers must team up

1164
00:59:38,923 --> 00:59:42,726
in groups of at least two
and host livestreams together.

1165
00:59:42,726 --> 00:59:44,628
The sales from those livestreams
will be combined,

1166
00:59:44,628 --> 00:59:46,554
and mission points will be awarded

1167
00:59:46,554 --> 00:59:49,900
to each team based on their sales ranking.

1168
00:59:49,900 --> 00:59:50,947
That's right.

1169
00:59:50,947 --> 00:59:53,820
Anyone can sell on their own.

1170
00:59:53,820 --> 00:59:57,341
But this is a competition
where you have to prove

1171
00:59:57,341 --> 01:00:00,411
you can work as a team
and build a livestream together.

1172
01:00:00,411 --> 01:00:03,154
Just like Round 3, Round 4 will be scored

1173
01:00:03,154 --> 01:00:04,848
[Round 4: Unity Or Fall]
out of 100 points.

1174
01:00:04,848 --> 01:00:07,918
50 for total sales, 40 for the mission,

1175
01:00:07,918 --> 01:00:11,722
and 10 from fan votes.

1176
01:00:11,722 --> 01:00:17,728
So you need selling power, teamwork,
and the fans on your side.

1177
01:00:17,728 --> 01:00:21,332
If we do a joint livestream,
all the sales from it count, right?

1178
01:00:21,332 --> 01:00:23,400
So those sales count
toward the 50 points for total sales,

1179
01:00:23,400 --> 01:00:25,502
and then we can also earn
another 40 mission points.

1180
01:00:26,721 --> 01:00:29,540
[JianHao Tan & Debbie Soon,
a couple who always go live together]

1181
01:00:29,540 --> 01:00:31,742
I was really happy. Because...

1182
01:00:31,742 --> 01:00:34,378
that's what I've been doing
for the past three rounds.

1183
01:00:34,378 --> 01:00:36,650
[Round 1 joint livestream]

1184
01:00:36,650 --> 01:00:38,182
[Round 2 joint livestream]
You guys all look so pretty.

1185
01:00:38,182 --> 01:00:40,221
Thank you for your support.

1186
01:00:40,221 --> 01:00:43,688
[Joint livestreams continued in Round 3]

1187
01:00:43,688 --> 01:00:47,124
Now we get extra points
just for doing what we already do.

1188
01:00:47,124 --> 01:00:50,427
I think this round is
a great opportunity for us.

1189
01:00:50,961 --> 01:00:54,732
[The rules for Round 4 aren't over yet]
There's one very important point here.

1190
01:00:54,732 --> 01:00:57,735
Selling content that isn't a livestream,
for example...

1191
01:00:57,735 --> 01:01:03,574
sales from Shorts you make together will
not count toward the mission score.

1192
01:01:03,574 --> 01:01:06,220
[Mission points can only be earned
through livestream selling]

1193
01:01:06,220 --> 01:01:08,078
Okay, good.

1194
01:01:08,078 --> 01:01:11,215
Then let's do this.
We'll work around your schedule.

1195
01:01:11,215 --> 01:01:16,324
Send me your schedule,
and I'll organize everything and let you know.

1196
01:01:16,324 --> 01:01:17,721
We'll do our best to make it work.

1197
01:01:17,721 --> 01:01:18,822
We live pretty close to each other.

1198
01:01:18,822 --> 01:01:22,953
Not close enough
to go live together every day, though.

1199
01:01:22,953 --> 01:01:27,698
[Former Thai idol & actor turned CEO]
Kathy's place is pretty spacious...

1200
01:01:27,698 --> 01:01:32,120
[Kathy's home studio with staff,
equipment, and plenty of space]

1201
01:01:32,120 --> 01:01:35,920
So we're planning to do
our joint livestreams at her house.

1202
01:01:35,920 --> 01:01:38,008
We'll go for our goal
with not just the 50 points for total sales,

1203
01:01:38,008 --> 01:01:39,721
but the extra 40 mission points too.

1204
01:01:39,721 --> 01:01:42,679
[Team Thailand has the perfect setup
for the joint livestream mission]

1205
01:01:42,679 --> 01:01:45,282
[Team Korea looks to climb back up the rankings]
If we just do...

1206
01:01:45,282 --> 01:01:49,254
what we've always done, make content

1207
01:01:49,254 --> 01:01:50,687
before the product launches,

1208
01:01:50,687 --> 01:01:54,958
then post content
and do a try-on livestream on launch day,

1209
01:01:54,958 --> 01:01:57,528
I feel like I could do just as well.

1210
01:01:57,528 --> 01:01:59,730
[1st generation influencer & actress]
We're all in this together.

1211
01:01:59,730 --> 01:02:03,434
This was exactly the mission I wanted.

1212
01:02:03,434 --> 01:02:05,836
All our team members are in Seoul.

1213
01:02:05,836 --> 01:02:08,005
It's so easy for us to get together.

1214
01:02:08,005 --> 01:02:11,208
I think we have an advantage.

1215
01:02:11,208 --> 01:02:13,777
I'm thinking about joining

1216
01:02:13,777 --> 01:02:16,521
the other members' livestreams

1217
01:02:16,521 --> 01:02:18,715
and being involved from start to finish.

1218
01:02:18,715 --> 01:02:20,669
[Team Korea has the advantage]

1219
01:02:21,151 --> 01:02:23,020
I think planning the schedule well is key.

1220
01:02:23,020 --> 01:02:24,388
For example, if the secondary account
goes live every day,

1221
01:02:24,388 --> 01:02:25,853
whoever's available can host,

1222
01:02:25,853 --> 01:02:26,857
and I can join in for special streams.

1223
01:02:26,857 --> 01:02:29,693
If you can come, come.

1224
01:02:29,693 --> 01:02:31,595
[Team China captain Ma Lingdao deep in thought]

1225
01:02:31,595 --> 01:02:33,864
I had a feeling this rule...

1226
01:02:33,864 --> 01:02:38,000
[Content planner of 50 billion won in sales]
wouldn't really work in our favor.

1227
01:02:38,000 --> 01:02:40,571
Because with the way things are
in China right now,

1228
01:02:40,571 --> 01:02:43,107
this kind of joint livestream is definitely...

1229
01:02:43,107 --> 01:02:45,075
[Team China members split
between China and South Korea]

1230
01:02:45,075 --> 01:02:47,165
[Scheduling joint livestreams could
be a challenge for Team China]

1231
01:02:47,654 --> 01:02:51,348
[Team Japan faces the same problem]

1232
01:02:51,348 --> 01:02:56,019
You're not coming to Japan in July?

1233
01:02:57,788 --> 01:03:00,724
Ryota lives in Thailand too,

1234
01:03:00,724 --> 01:03:04,995
so coordinating schedules is
difficult in a lot of ways.

1235
01:03:04,995 --> 01:03:08,332
Kii Chan also goes to Korea for shoots,

1236
01:03:08,332 --> 01:03:12,603
so it's hard to find a day
when everyone's in Japan.

1237
01:03:12,603 --> 01:03:17,441
[Team Japan members scattered
across different locations and schedules]

1238
01:03:17,441 --> 01:03:23,614
[Another challenge Team Japan must overcome]

1239
01:03:23,614 --> 01:03:27,384
The top teams must hold
their ground all the way to the end,

1240
01:03:27,384 --> 01:03:31,054
while the lower-ranked teams can't afford
to miss a single opportunity.

1241
01:03:31,054 --> 01:03:34,195
They have to turn things around this round.

1242
01:03:34,195 --> 01:03:39,463
Round 4, Unity Or Fall,
where no one can let their guard down

1243
01:03:39,463 --> 01:03:42,098
for even a moment, starts now.

1244
01:03:43,800 --> 01:03:47,721
[Round 4 Unity Or Fall Starts]

1245
01:03:47,721 --> 01:03:51,642
Will you survive together,
or fall apart on your own?

1246
01:03:51,642 --> 01:03:54,478
[United we stand, divided we fall]
This was exactly the mission I wanted.

1247
01:03:54,478 --> 01:03:57,621
[Going all in in Round 4 to reclaim X1]

1248
01:03:57,621 --> 01:03:58,820
What should I show them first?

1249
01:03:58,820 --> 01:04:00,984
[Team Korea is built for this mission]

1250
01:04:00,984 --> 01:04:02,688
I'm just going to stay in Korea.

1251
01:04:02,688 --> 01:04:04,388
[Crossing borders for the mission]
I'm all set to head straight to Korea.

1252
01:04:04,388 --> 01:04:07,357
[Team China is more determined than ever]

1253
01:04:07,357 --> 01:04:11,128
[A do-or-die comeback from the brink]

1254
01:04:11,128 --> 01:04:12,930
[Team Vietnam united by sheer determination]

1255
01:04:12,930 --> 01:04:15,799
It's what we've been doing
for the past three rounds.

1256
01:04:15,799 --> 01:04:18,936
[Singapore & Malaysia: Unbeatable Teamwork]
We have to move on. Faster!

1257
01:04:18,936 --> 01:04:21,738
We'll now announce the final tiers for Round 4.

1258
01:04:21,738 --> 01:04:23,707
[Which team will show the best teamwork?]

1259
01:04:23,707 --> 01:04:26,776
I think we can make X1 this time.
